bers greater than 104,&#10;stands at the forefront of modern nuclear physics. These&#10;unique and highly unstable nuclei exist primarily due to the&#10;quantum shell effects, which provide an additi...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: chemical_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Transforming Separation Science with Single-Molecule&#10;Methods&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['single-entity trajectory analysis',&#10;'stochastic transport and residence-time modeling', 'bottom-up&#10;multiscale mechanistic modeling of separation', 'rare-event&#10;detection and statistical inference from sparse single-&#10;molecule/single-atom observations', 'mapping microscopic&#10;interaction dynamics to macroscopic capture/separation&#10;efficiency']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate paper's single-molecule&#10;separation framework to superheavy-element chemistry by&#10;modeling chemical capture, transport, and identification as a&#10;stochastic single-atom process with adsorption/desorption,&#10;diffusion, decay competition, and event-by-event inferen...&#10;justification: The candidate paper's core abstraction—using&#10;single-entity observations to replace empirical optimization&#10;with mechanistic, multiscale models of separation—maps&#10;directly onto the superheavy-element bottleneck of time-&#10;critical single-atom capture and chemical identification.&#10;abstract: Empirical optimization of the multiscale parameters&#10;underlying chromatographic and membrane separations leads to&#10;enormous resource waste and production costs. A bottom-up&#10;approach to understand the physical phenomena underlying&#10;challenges in separations is possible with single...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 4&#10;domain: chemical_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Evaluating the use of a continuous approximation for&#10;model-based quantification of pulsed chemical exchange&#10;saturation transfer (CEST)&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['continuous approximation of pulsed&#10;exchange processes', 'model-based quantification of transfer&#10;between interacting states or pools', 'time-dependent&#10;exchange/survival modeling under limited observables']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the continuous-approximation framework&#10;to model the superheavy-element pipeline as a set of coupled&#10;state pools—production, survival against fission, decay,&#10;chemical capture, and identification—where pulsed reaction and&#10;transport steps are represented by effective contin...&#10;justification: Although from chemical-exchange MRI, the&#10;candidate’s core abstraction—approximating pulsed multi-state&#10;exchange with a continuous model for quantitative&#10;inference—maps structurally onto the problem of linking rare&#10;production events, survival/decay dynamics, and time-critical&#10;s...&#10;abstract:&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: statistics&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Uncertainty quantified discovery of chemical reaction&#10;systems via Bayesian scientific machine learning&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Bayesian uncertainty quantification over&#10;discovered reaction pathways', 'Physically interpretable&#10;neural representation of a reaction network', 'Digital-twin&#10;modeling of coupled reaction/transport kinetics', 'Inference&#10;from sparse, time-resolved species/event data']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the Bayesian CRNN idea to a unified&#10;superheavy-element 'reaction network digital twin' whose nodes&#10;and edges represent fusion/evaporation, quasifission, decay&#10;chains, chemical capture, and transport steps, with Bayesian&#10;posteriors over rates, cross sections, survival pro...&#10;justification: The candidate paper’s core abstraction is&#10;uncertainty-quantified, interpretable discovery of reaction-&#10;network dynamics from time-resolved data. That maps&#10;structurally onto the superheavy-element problem, which is&#10;also a coupled network of production, survival, decay, and&#10;chemi...&#10;