e_id: 3&#10;domain: chemical_engineering&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Transforming Separation Science with Single-Molecule&#10;Methods&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['single-entity trajectory analysis',&#10;'stochastic transport and residence-time modeling', 'bottom-up&#10;multiscale mechanistic modeling of separation', 'rare-event&#10;detection and statistical inference from sparse single-&#10;molecule/single-atom observations', 'mapping microscopic&#10;interaction dynamics to macroscopic capture/separation&#10;efficiency']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate paper's single-molecule&#10;separation framework to superheavy-element chemistry by&#10;modeling chemical capture, transport, and identification as a&#10;stochastic single-atom process with adsorption/desorption,&#10;diffusion, decay competition, and event-by-event inferen...&#10;justification: The candidate paper's core abstraction—using&#10;single-entity observations to replace empirical optimization&#10;with mechanistic, multiscale models of separation—maps&#10;directly onto the superheavy-element bottleneck of time-&#10;critical single-atom capture and chemical identification.&#10;abstract: Empirical optimization of the multiscale parameters&#10;underlying chromatographic and membrane separations leads to&#10;enormous resource waste and production costs. A bottom-up&#10;approach to understand the physical phenomena underlying&#10;challenges in separations is possible with single...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 1&#10;domain: same_field&#10;radius: R1&#10;title: Colliding heavy nuclei take multiple identities on the&#10;path to fusion&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Pre-capture mass and charge transfer as&#10;a branching multi-identity process', 'Ensemble of projectile-&#10;target partitions rather than a single entrance channel',&#10;'Partition-dependent fusion probabilities linking early&#10;collision dynamics to final compound-nucleus formation',&#10;'Framework for calibrating capture/fusion models against&#10;observed transfer-partition complexity']&#10;combination_plan: Integrate a stochastic pre-fusion transfer&#10;network into the superheavy-element discovery framework, where&#10;heavy-ion collisions generate multiple evolving nuclear&#10;identities with partition-dependent capture, fusion, survival,&#10;and decay probabilities. These branching outcomes ca...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a mechanistic&#10;abstraction for the original problem’s reaction-choice and&#10;quasifission bottleneck: instead of treating fusion as a&#10;single deterministic pathway, it models early collision&#10;dynamics as a complex branching process with many possible&#10;nuc...&#10;abstract: The properties of superheavy elements probe extremes&#10;of physics and chemistry. They are synthesised at accelerator&#10;laboratories using nuclear fusion, where two atomic nuclei&#10;collide, stick together (capture), then with low probability&#10;evolve to a compact superheavy nucleus. Th..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="12010" width="620" height="1752" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: resumed&#10;idea_count: 1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="13862" width="220" height="90" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Verification First-Passage Assay for the Verifiable&#10;Completion Boundary of the Periodic Table&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: The question whether the periodic table can ever be&#10;complete is not only a synthesis problem; it is also a&#10;verification problem because IUPAC/IUPAP recognition depends on&#10;evidence that can become extremely difficult to obtain for few&#10;short-lived atoms [Author et al.,&#10;2020](https://openalex.org/W3048546628). Hot-fusion reaction&#10;surveys identify plausible projectile-target routes toward&#10;elements beyond Z = 118 and p...&#10;methods: 1. Verification first-passage estimand: We define a&#10;latent state x = (Z, A, reaction channel) and event-level&#10;observables including decay-chain graph, decay energies/times,&#10;optional characteristic X-rays, and time-stamped&#10;transport/arrival data under a controlled intervention u. The&#10;verification first-passage time tau_v is the earliest time at&#10;which the posterior Bayes factor for one Z against the best&#10;competing Z exceeds a pre-registered threshold; the minimum&#10;verification capability C_min is the smallest expec...&#10;novelty_justification: The closest existing combination is the&#10;IUPAC/IUPAP discovery criteria plus the UniCell/atmospheric-&#10;pressure gas-flow simulation study, with hot-fusion entrance-&#10;channel surveys and superheavy stability calculations supplying&#10;production and nuclear priors. Those references already connect&#10;superheavy synthesis, decay-chain verification, and gas-phase&#10;transport/chemistry. The proposal adds a formal verification&#10;first...&#10;improvement_suggestions: ['Sharpen the mechanistic claim by&#10;making decay itself perturb transport, for example using alpha&#10;decay, fission fragments, recoil charge-state changes, or decay-&#10;induced desorption to create decay-gated residence-time&#10;signatures that are intrinsic to superheavy atoms rather than&#10;generic externally imposed modulation.', 'Introduce a conceptual&#10;verification-boundary criterion, such as a provable&#10;identifiability or verification horizon, that specifies when no&#10;admissible modulation, chemistry, or beam-time budget can reach&#10;the required Bayes factor because of overlapping adsorption&#10;enthalpies, short half-lives, and background; then design&#10;adaptive modulation to approach that bound.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="13862" width="680" height="834" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: fusion-evaporation reaction cross sections for&#10;synthesizing element 119&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'fusion evaporation', 'score': 10},&#10;{'text': 'evaporation reaction', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'reaction cross', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'cross sections',&#10;'score': 7}, {'text': 'sections synthesizing', 'score':&#10;6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. /sup 18/O + /sup 12/C fusion-evaporation reaction&#10;(1980) [score=0.9552]&#10;Abstract: A study of the /sup 18/O + /sup 12/C fusion&#10;evaporation reaction has been undertaken for 2 reasons: to&#10;make a systematic study of the formation cross section for&#10;each individual evaporation residue over a broad&#10;excitation energy region in the compound nucleus /sup&#10;30/Si:30 to...&#10;&#10;2. Hot atom reactions involving multivalent and univalent&#10;species. Progress report, February 1974--January 1975&#10;(1974) [score=0.573]&#10;Abstract: abstraction reactions. The reaction probability&#10;curve for the H-abstraction from PH$sub 3$ to give $sup&#10;32$PH$sub 3$ covers an extremely wide range but has a&#10;threshold somewhat above the thermal energy range, while&#10;the reaction probability curve for the F-abstraction from&#10;PF$s...&#10;&#10;3. Mechanisms Suppressing Superheavy Element Yields in&#10;Cold Fusion Reactions (2019) [score=0.5374]&#10;Abstract: Superheavy elements are formed in fusion&#10;reactions which are hindered by fast nonequilibrium&#10;processes. To quantify these, mass-angle distributions and&#10;cross sections have been measured, at beam energies from&#10;below-barrier to 25% above, for the reactions of ^{48}Ca,&#10;^{50}Ti, a...&#10;&#10;4. Benchmark Calculation for Double Differential Cross&#10;Section of (&lt;i&gt;p, xn&lt;/i&gt;) and (&lt;i&gt;p, xp&lt;/i&gt;) Reaction&#10;(1994) [score=0.5274]&#10;Abstract: KEYWORDS: benchmarksdouble differential cross&#10;sectionsintermediate energy 25–1,600&#10;MeVleadzirconiumNUCLEUSHETC-3STEPintranuclear cascade&#10;evaporationhigh energy fissionpreequilibriumclosed form&#10;exciton modellevel density parameter&#10;&#10;5. Fe2(CO)9 (1969) [score=0.5252]&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;6. The Multi-dimensional Langevin Approach to the&#10;Description of Fusion-fission Reactions (2002)&#10;[score=0.5188]&#10;Abstract: The two stage approach to the description of&#10;fusion-fission reactions is suggested. On each stage&#10;(fusion or fission) the tree-dimensional Langevin equation&#10;for the variables describing the shape of nuclear system&#10;is solved. The results obtained on the first stage are&#10;used as...&#10;&#10;7. The Chemistry of Transactinide Elements-Experimental&#10;Achievements and Perspectives (2002) [score=0.5188]&#10;Abstract: The