lation environment—a Python library for&#10;working with atoms (2017)&#10;Abstract: The atomic simulation environment (ASE) is a&#10;software package written in the Python programming&#10;language with the aim of setting up, steering, and&#10;analyzing atomistic simulations. In ASE, tasks are fully&#10;scripted in Python. The powerful syntax of Python combined&#10;with the NumPy...&#10;&#10;5. Microstructural development in equiatomic&#10;multicomponent alloys (2004)&#10;Abstract: N/A&#10;&#10;6. Development of a DTPA Soil Test for Zinc, Iron,&#10;Manganese, and Copper (1978)&#10;Abstract: Abstract A DTPA soil test was developed to&#10;identify near‐neutral and calcareous soils with&#10;insufficient available Zn, Fe, Mn, or Cu for maximum&#10;yields of crops. The extractant consists of 0.005 M DTPA&#10;(diethylenetriaminepentaacetic acid), 0.1 M&#10;triethanolamine, and 0.01 M CaCl...&#10;&#10;7. Synthesis of a New Element with Atomic Number Z = 117&#10;(2010)&#10;Abstract: The discovery of a new chemical element with&#10;atomic number Z=117 is reported. The isotopes (293)117 and&#10;(294)117 were produced in fusion reactions between (48)Ca&#10;and (249)Bk. Decay chains involving 11 new nuclei were&#10;identified by means of the Dubna gas-filled recoil&#10;separator...&#10;&#10;8. Atomic number and crystallographic contrast images with&#10;the SEM: a review of backscattered electron techniques&#10;(1987)&#10;Abstract: Abstract Backscattered electrons (BSE) are&#10;incident electrons reflected back from a target specimen&#10;and imaged with the scanning electron microscope (SEM).&#10;Three distinct BSE signals exist: atomic number or&#10;Z-contrast, in which composition determines image&#10;contrast; orientatio...&#10;&#10;9. Effective Atomic Number and Energy Absorption in&#10;Tissues (1946)&#10;Abstract: An X-ray absorption method, using Ross balanced&#10;filters, is applied to measure the effective atomic number&#10;of excised body tissues. The results are used to